+## Windows process identity
+
+The desktop and app-server queries share embedded PowerShell scripts from
+`src/codex/windows-process-identity.ts`. A single CIM snapshot supplies parent and command metadata;
+a native process handle supplies token SID, executable path and creation time for the same generation.
+The desktop query publishes only current-user images inside the discovered package boundary and retains
+the base64 command-line column used by compatibility-context capture. An unreadable identity remains
+unknown, rather than an empty process list. The app-server query keeps the existing narrow candidate
+patterns and emits the incomplete-enumeration sentinel if a still-live identity cannot be verified.
+The existing query deadlines, ancestry protection and quit/relaunch ladder remain unchanged.
+The scripts are TypeScript literals, so compiled distributions need no adjacent PowerShell resource files.
+`tests/clients/windows-process-identity.test.ts` covers the shared query and parser contracts;
+the Windows-only tests in the existing desktop/app-server suites exercise PowerShell selection and native enumeration.
 
